# Supabase / RLS

- Every tenant table has `organization_id` unless it is auth-global by design.
- Enable RLS and create explicit policies in the same migration or immediately following migration.
- Authorization derives from `auth.uid()` membership and role, never `members[0]`.
- A client-supplied organization id is only context; membership/RLS must still authorize it.
- Secretary must have no SELECT policy on clinical-only tables.
- Prefer Supabase generated TypeScript types after migrations.
- service-role client exists only in server-only module and is used narrowly.
- Storage bucket policies must mirror tenant/role rules.
- Write RLS adversarial tests with a real/local Supabase Auth path.

- RLS membership helpers that use SECURITY DEFINER must be STABLE, use `SET search_path = ''`, schema-qualify referenced objects, use `auth.uid()` internally, and expose only minimal EXECUTE privileges.
- `practice_settings.secretary_finance_access` (`none|view|manage`) is enforced in financial RLS; UI visibility is never the enforcement.
